From: Andrea Campanella <emuboy85@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ps2gs: Map the packet buffer uncached accelerated

The library builds each frame's packets in the buffer it maps from
/dev/ps2gs: 256 KiB written once a frame and read by the DMA. With a
cached mapping, each 64-byte line the program writes is fetched from
memory first (the data cache is 8 KiB, write allocate), at more than a
hundred cycles a line. A profile of the library had a third of its time
in the vertex copy, which is thirteen stores.

The EE has an uncached accelerated mode (C = 7 in the TLB): a store goes
to the write buffer, sequential stores merge into one burst, nothing is
fetched. The homebrew SDK builds its DMA packets that way. Give the
R5900 that mode as its write-combine attribute, map the buffer with it,
and write back and invalidate the cached alias once after the zeroing,
so that no stale line can come down over the program's data. The send
needs no cache writeback any more, only an empty write buffer.

PS2GS_VERSION is 3. A library that sees 3 puts a sync before each send
and before it reads the buffer back.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [PlayStation 2 port]
---
diff --git a/drivers/ps2/gs-dev.c b/drivers/ps2/gs-dev.c
index 63913f3..62ecb26 100644
--- a/drivers/ps2/gs-dev.c
+++ b/drivers/ps2/gs-dev.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 
 #include <uapi/linux/ps2gs.h>
 
-#define PS2GS_VERSION		2	/* 2: PS2GS_IOC_RECEIVE */
+#define PS2GS_VERSION		3	/* 2: PS2GS_IOC_RECEIVE. 3: the buffer is uncached accelerated */
 /* The buffer taken at the start: the size the library asks for by default */
 #define PS2GS_RESERVED_BUFFER	(256 * 1024)
 
@@ -341,7 +341,12 @@ static int ps2gs_send(struct ps2gs_file *f, const struct ps2gs_send *s)
 
 	ch = &ps2gs.channel[s->channel];
 
-	dma_cache_wback((unsigned long)f->virt + s->offset, len);
+	/*
+	 * The program writes the buffer through an uncached accelerated
+	 * mapping (see ps2gs_mmap), so the cache holds none of it. The
+	 * write buffer of the CPU must be empty before the DMA reads.
+	 */
+	wmb();
 
 	mutex_lock(&ps2gs.lock);
 
@@ -536,7 +541,18 @@ static int ps2gs_mmap(struct file *file, struct vm_area_struct *vma)
 		f->reserved = false;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Uncached accelerated (C = 7 in the TLB): a store goes to the
+	 * write buffer and from there to memory in 64-byte bursts, with no
+	 * fetch of the cache line first. The library writes each frame's
+	 * packets into this buffer once and never reads them back, so a
+	 * cached mapping only paid for the fetches: a quarter of its time
+	 * for each vertex. The zeroing above went through the cache, so
+	 * that goes out and away before the program writes underneath it.
+	 */
+	dma_cache_wback_inv((unsigned long)page_address(pages), size);
 	vma->vm_flags |= VM_IO | VM_DONTEXPAND | VM_DONTDUMP;
+	vma->vm_page_prot = pgprot_writecombine(vma->vm_page_prot);
 	err = remap_pfn_range(vma, vma->vm_start, page_to_pfn(pages),
 		size, vma->vm_page_prot);
 	if (err) {
diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
index 6169e33..5a947b1 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -1482,6 +1482,8 @@ static inline void cpu_probe_legacy(struct cpuinfo_mips *c, unsigned int cpu)
 		c->options = R4K_OPTS | MIPS_CPU_DIVEC | MIPS_CPU_FPU |
 			     MIPS_CPU_32FPR;
 		c->tlbsize = 48;
+		/* C = 7 in the TLB: uncached accelerated, for DMA packet buffers */
+		c->writecombine = _CACHE_UNCACHED_ACCELERATED;
 		break;
 	case PRID_IMP_NEVADA:
 		c->cputype = CPU_NEVADA;
